[0.991,"o","ov stack deploy openvidu-e2e-oci-ce-a123302 --cloud oracle --oci-region \"$OCI_REGION\" --oci-compartment \"$OCI_COMPARTMENT_OCID\" --edition community --certificate-type selfsigned --mode auto -y\r\n"]
[2.481,"o","warning: the stack publishes into the vault *** (--oci-vault), which is not its own. Its secrets have fixed names (OPENVIDU_URL, the credentials, the license, the stack's access), so two stacks in one vault mix them; every deploy adds versions to the same secrets until Oracle refuses more (LimitExceeded) and the stack never publishes; and a destroy leaves this stack's credentials in it. Give every stack a vault of its own: leave --oci-vault out and the stack creates one\r\n"]
[8.893,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so the command that continues this deploy needs no flags\r\n"]
[8.894,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nThis is what ov does in your Oracle Cloud tenancy (region eu-madrid-1, compartment ***); --debug shows every command:\r\n\r\n  1. Template: render the single node template into .openvidu/oracle/tf-oracle-openvidu-singlenode.tf\r\n     and its variables into .openvidu/oracle/openvidu.auto.tfvars.json (0600)\r\n  2. Machines: create the machine, which installs OpenVidu Community on itself with Terraform (about 3 minutes, then OpenVidu installs)\r\n  3. Wait for OpenVidu to answer, read the stack over SSH and register this directory as the stack\r\n\r\nWarning: the stack publishes into the vault *** (--oci-vault), which is not its own. Its secrets have fixed names (OPENVIDU_URL, the credentials, the license, the stack's access), so two stacks in one vault mix them; every deploy adds versions to the same secrets until Oracle refuses more (LimitExceeded) and the stack never publishes; and a destroy leaves this stack's credentials in it. Give every stack a vault of its own: leave --oci-vault out and the stack creates one.\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n\r\n▶ Create the machines on Oracle Cloud…\r\n   · initialize Terraform in .openvidu/oracle (downloads the provider)\r\n"]
[44.62,"o","   · apply .openvidu/oracle (this returns when Terraform is done)\r\n"]
[86.939,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so `ov stack destroy` removes it even if the wait below fails\r\n   ✓ Create the machines on Oracle Cloud\r\n\r\n▶ Wait for the machines to deploy OpenVidu…\r\n"]
